  "body": "Release cut for **CamCraft 0.17.0** (minor: 32 feat, 32 fix since v0.16.0; nothing breaking, project file stays v58).\n\n## What's in this PR\n- `docs: 0.17.0 release notes; changelog`: the 0.17.0 section in `RELEASE_NOTES.md` (not breaking, but posted G-code changes for existing machines are listed first; New / Fixed / Changed / Process changes 1-10 / Known issues), 61 `CHANGELOG.md` rows from the merged PRs' `Changelog:` lines, and the 70 `docs/decisions/*.md` files gathered into `RECOMMENDED.md` under v0.17.0 (`cargo xtask decisions`).\n- `chore(release): 0.17.0 - release` and `chore(release): sync Cargo.lock to 0.17.0`: the version bump (Cargo.lock: version lines only, asserted by the release tool).\n\n## How it was cut\n- `cargo xtask release --version 0.17.0 --no-tag --installer` on this branch (the first real run of the xtask release tool, #749).\n- **Release gate:** 12 of 13 steps passed on this exact tree (every debug suite, ui, clippy `-D warnings`, the motion and app heavy lanes in release; 54 min). Step 13, the ui **pixel snapshot lane**, failed on 3 goldens: icon antialiasing in the main window (~800 px, dark and light) and the tool editor's new wider layout with its Tool body column (~229k px). The maintainer judged the pixel goldens unreliable and approved `--skip-gate` for the rest of the cut; their structural twins pass. Removing the pixel lane is a follow-up after the tag.\n- Build, `post.exe` version check (0.17.0) and the zip (`camcraft-0.17.0-win-x64.zip`, 86 files) done locally. Not signed (no certificate configured); no local installer (Inno Setup not installed here) - `release.yml` builds the installer and publishes from the tag.\n\n## After merge\nTag the merge commit `v0.17.0` (after `git diff <branch tip> main` is empty), push the tag (fires `release.yml`), and comment `shipped in v0.17.0` on the issues closed since v0.16.0.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
